WEBVTT

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:36.502
We need this completely filled.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.594
We don't have time
to haggle over price.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.105
Understood.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:45.533
Captain.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.732
Janeway to Voy...

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:07.664
Get up!

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.574
Get away from her!

00:03:19.029 --> 00:03:20.121
Commander...

00:03:20.164 --> 00:03:21.563
any word on that tellerium?

00:03:21.599 --> 00:03:22.588
Not yet.

00:03:22.633 --> 00:03:23.725
How bad is it?

00:03:23.768 --> 00:03:26.396
The antimatter reaction rate
is down to 12 percent.

00:03:26.437 --> 00:03:27.870
If it drops below nine,

00:03:27.905 --> 00:03:29.065
the plasma injectors
will lock up

00:03:29.106 --> 00:03:31.404
and we'll never be able
to reinitialize the nacelles.

00:03:31.442 --> 00:03:32.739
Options?

00:03:32.777 --> 00:03:35.041
If we're going to reduce
our power demands even further,

00:03:35.079 --> 00:03:36.979
we're going to have
to drop the shields.

00:03:37.014 --> 00:03:38.709
I don't want to leave
the ship defenseless

00:03:38.749 --> 00:03:40.273
this close to a hostile planet.

00:03:40.317 --> 00:03:42.478
All other systems
are already off-line.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:43.748
Life support is at minimal.

00:03:43.788 --> 00:03:45.221
You asked for options.

00:03:45.256 --> 00:03:46.587
That's our last one.

00:03:48.259 --> 00:03:50.193
All right,
power down the shields.

00:03:58.903 --> 00:04:00.768
That helped.

00:04:00.805 --> 00:04:02.170
It's only a matter of time.

00:04:02.206 --> 00:04:04.140
There's nothing more we can do
without the tellerium.

00:04:04.175 --> 00:04:06.143
Neelix to Voyager.

00:04:06.177 --> 00:04:07.371
Yes, Neelix.

00:04:07.411 --> 00:04:09.402
The rest of the away team
is gone, Commander.

00:04:09.447 --> 00:04:10.744
They've been taken by the Mokra.

00:04:10.781 --> 00:04:12.976
What do you want me to do?

00:04:13.017 --> 00:04:14.109
Did you get the tellerium?

00:04:14.151 --> 00:04:15.709
Yes, I have it.

00:04:15.753 --> 00:04:17.050
Then we need you here.

00:04:17.087 --> 00:04:19.055
Prepare to beam directly
to Engineering.

00:04:19.089 --> 00:04:22.217
Rerouting emergency power
to Transporter Room 2.

00:04:22.259 --> 00:04:23.556
And...

00:04:23.594 --> 00:04:24.993
energizing.

00:04:31.802 --> 00:04:34.600
Chakotay to away team.
Captain, can you hear me?

00:04:35.639 --> 00:04:37.038
Unlock the control conduit.

00:04:38.476 --> 00:04:40.376
Tuvok, Torres,

00:04:40.411 --> 00:04:42.402
please respond.

00:04:42.446 --> 00:04:43.572
Keep an eye on the flow rate.

00:04:43.614 --> 00:04:44.603
Yes, sir.

00:04:46.517 --> 00:04:48.985
Rate's holding steady.

00:04:49.019 --> 00:04:51.487
The reaction rate
is stabilized

00:04:51.589 --> 00:04:53.079
at 13 percent.

00:04:53.123 --> 00:04:57.116
Up to 15... 18.

00:04:57.161 --> 00:04:58.753
It worked then.
We're all right?

00:04:58.796 --> 00:04:59.763
Maybe.

00:04:59.797 --> 00:05:01.264
Once the rate is up to normal,

00:05:01.298 --> 00:05:03.766
we'll try getting
the warp drive back on line.

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:05.029
Then we'll see
if there was any damage.

00:05:05.069 --> 00:05:07.629
Begin rerouting power
back to all key systems.

00:05:07.671 --> 00:05:09.161
What happened down there?

00:05:09.206 --> 00:05:11.606
I don't know, exactly.

00:05:11.642 --> 00:05:13.041
I went in the shop,
completed the trade,

00:05:13.077 --> 00:05:15.238
then I heard weapons fire
on the street.

00:05:15.279 --> 00:05:16.439
By the time I got out there,

00:05:16.547 --> 00:05:18.174
the Captain
and the others were gone.

00:05:18.215 --> 00:05:19.443
Are you sure it was the Mokra?

00:05:19.517 --> 00:05:21.815
I spoke to witnesses
on the street.

00:05:21.852 --> 00:05:23.820
They said it was quite a fight.

00:05:23.854 --> 00:05:26.049
Any idea how the Mokra
knew you were down there?

00:05:27.525 --> 00:05:30.119
Someone must have told them
we were coming.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.924
The Mokra have informants
everywhere.

00:05:32.963 --> 00:05:34.863
Could your contact
be one of them?

00:05:34.899 --> 00:05:37.390
I don't think I would have
made it back here

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:39.368
with the tellerium
if he had been.

00:05:39.403 --> 00:05:41.462
Besides, he's involved

00:05:41.505 --> 00:05:43.063
with the Alsaurian
resistance movement.

00:05:43.107 --> 00:05:44.904
He would never help the Mokra.

00:05:44.942 --> 00:05:46.773
They've probably got
the resistance movement

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.107
under surveillance.

00:05:48.145 --> 00:05:49.373
Commander.

00:05:49.413 --> 00:05:51.506
I think we're ready
to give the engines a try.

00:05:57.021 --> 00:05:59.319
I'm opening
the plasma injectors.

00:06:08.566 --> 00:06:11.660
Warp engines are back on line.

00:06:11.702 --> 00:06:13.363
All systems normal.

00:06:13.404 --> 00:06:14.962
Good work, Mr. Kim.

00:06:15.005 --> 00:06:16.370
Mr. Neelix, you're with me.

00:06:16.407 --> 00:06:18.898
I think it's time
we contact the Mokra.

00:06:21.211 --> 00:06:22.974
Mr. Paris, set a new course.

00:06:23.013 --> 00:06:24.378
Bring us out
from behind the moon

00:06:24.415 --> 00:06:26.610
and establish a standard orbit
around the planet... slowly.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:27.947
We don't want
to look aggressive.

00:06:27.985 --> 00:06:29.247
Yes, sir.

00:06:29.286 --> 00:06:32.187
What kind of response should
we expect when they see us?

00:06:32.222 --> 00:06:34.747
The Mokra are paranoid
and hostile.

00:06:34.792 --> 00:06:36.726
They have little use
for diplomacy.

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:37.749
I wouldn't be surprised

00:06:37.795 --> 00:06:41.060
if they started shooting
at us immediately.

00:06:41.098 --> 00:06:43.658
We'll be in full view
of the planet in a few seconds.

00:06:50.407 --> 00:06:52.705
Their orbital sensor net
has picked us up.

00:06:52.743 --> 00:06:54.574
They're scanning the ship.

00:06:56.914 --> 00:06:58.404
We're being hailed.

00:06:58.449 --> 00:06:59.438
On screen.

00:07:00.884 --> 00:07:04.718
I am Third Magistrate Augris
of the Mokra Order.

00:07:04.755 --> 00:07:07.849
Commander Chakotay of the
Federation Starship Voyager.

00:07:07.891 --> 00:07:10.587
May I assume
you're seeking permission

00:07:10.628 --> 00:07:12.596
to conduct business with us?

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:14.359
No. Some of my crew members

00:07:14.398 --> 00:07:16.025
have already been
to the surface.

00:07:16.066 --> 00:07:17.727
We've lost contact with them.

00:07:17.768 --> 00:07:19.429
I see.

00:07:19.536 --> 00:07:22.835
You must have been unaware
of our regulations.

00:07:22.873 --> 00:07:25.774
I'll transfer a complete copy
for future reference.

00:07:25.809 --> 00:07:28.801
I have reason to believe
they're being detained.

00:07:28.846 --> 00:07:30.279
Detained?

00:07:30.314 --> 00:07:32.043
That's possible.

00:07:32.082 --> 00:07:33.606
I'll look into it for you.

00:07:33.651 --> 00:07:35.812
I'll contact you shortly.

00:07:35.853 --> 00:07:37.252
Thank you.

00:07:39.657 --> 00:07:41.682
He's not like any Mokra
I've ever met.

00:07:41.725 --> 00:07:43.750
I can't believe
he'll really help us.

00:07:43.794 --> 00:07:45.853
If there's any chance
for a diplomatic solution,

00:07:45.896 --> 00:07:47.022
we have to pursue it.

00:07:47.064 --> 00:07:49.589
In the meantime, I want
continuous scans of the surface.

00:07:49.633 --> 00:07:51.658
Standard search pattern.

00:08:10.788 --> 00:08:12.653
I advise caution.

00:08:13.657 --> 00:08:15.887
There's a control circuit there.
I can see it.

00:08:21.031 --> 00:08:23.056
If only we knew
that Neelix made it

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:25.034
back to the ship
with the tellerium,

00:08:25.069 --> 00:08:27.435
then at least this
would be worth it.

00:08:27.504 --> 00:08:31.531
I regret I have no such
reassurance to offer you.

00:08:31.575 --> 00:08:33.338
We don't even know what
happened to the Captain.

00:08:33.377 --> 00:08:35.436
She might have been killed
out there on the street.

00:08:35.546 --> 00:08:37.013
That is possible.

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:40.617
It is also possible

00:08:40.651 --> 00:08:42.448
that she has safely
returned to Voyager.

00:08:42.553 --> 00:08:43.918
We have insufficient evidence

00:08:43.954 --> 00:08:46.388
to dismiss either conclusion.

00:08:48.292 --> 00:08:49.953
I guess that's the Vulcan way

00:08:49.993 --> 00:08:52.052
of telling me
to hope for the best.

00:09:29.967 --> 00:09:31.696
Look who's awake.

00:09:33.003 --> 00:09:34.903
Just rest.

00:09:34.938 --> 00:09:37.099
You must be thirsty.

00:09:37.141 --> 00:09:40.042
Maybe hungry?

00:09:40.077 --> 00:09:42.045
For a little something?

00:09:45.983 --> 00:09:47.610
Oh, what shall I make?

00:09:47.651 --> 00:09:51.382
What, what can I make?
What, what?

00:09:53.557 --> 00:09:55.320
Oh...

00:09:59.229 --> 00:10:00.218
Where am I?

00:10:00.264 --> 00:10:02.926
Oh, it hasn't been that long.

00:10:02.966 --> 00:10:05.730
I wish I had some...
There.

00:10:05.769 --> 00:10:08.101
This will do.

00:10:12.042 --> 00:10:14.067
T-To drink.

00:10:20.317 --> 00:10:21.614
Thank you.

00:10:21.652 --> 00:10:23.483
I'll fix you some soup.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:27.479
Now, just... lie down.

00:10:27.524 --> 00:10:28.616
You're very kind, but I have...

00:10:28.659 --> 00:10:30.627
It's all right.
You're safe now.

00:10:30.661 --> 00:10:31.355
I really can't...

00:10:31.395 --> 00:10:33.659
Shh, shh.

00:10:33.697 --> 00:10:35.187
Don't worry.

00:10:35.232 --> 00:10:37.132
Everything's all right now.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:42.001
My little girl is home.

00:11:11.334 --> 00:11:12.596
I'm very grateful

00:11:12.635 --> 00:11:13.829
for everything
you've done for me.

00:11:13.869 --> 00:11:15.700
But you know there's
nothing I wouldn't do

00:11:15.738 --> 00:11:16.705
for my sweet Ralkana.

00:11:16.739 --> 00:11:20.334
My name is Kathryn Janeway.

00:11:20.376 --> 00:11:21.775
"Kathryn"?

00:11:21.811 --> 00:11:24.211
That's an unusual name.

00:11:24.247 --> 00:11:26.215
Very pretty.

00:11:26.249 --> 00:11:27.682
I-I like it.

00:11:27.717 --> 00:11:29.742
I am a starship Captain.

00:11:29.785 --> 00:11:33.516
It is very important
that I contact my ship.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:35.989
Wonderful.

00:11:36.025 --> 00:11:41.554
Captain... Kathryn
of a glorious starship.

00:11:42.898 --> 00:11:44.331
Then what happens?

00:11:44.367 --> 00:11:45.664
Go on.

00:11:45.701 --> 00:11:46.725
I'm listening.

00:11:46.769 --> 00:11:47.736
I love your stories.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.203
It's not a story.

00:11:49.238 --> 00:11:51.331
It's a request.

00:11:51.374 --> 00:11:53.638
May I use
your communications equipment?

00:11:53.676 --> 00:11:55.473
Communications...

00:11:55.511 --> 00:11:58.105
Uh, we're not supposed
to have any of that.

00:11:58.147 --> 00:11:59.842
The Mokra don't allow it.

00:11:59.882 --> 00:12:02.077
They can't have control
of everything.

00:12:02.118 --> 00:12:04.814
Surely there's someone
who has an illegal transmitter.

00:12:04.854 --> 00:12:08.756
I know what you'd like...
some talsa root soup.

00:12:10.559 --> 00:12:11.457
Can you at least tell me

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:12.788
what happened
to the other people

00:12:12.828 --> 00:12:13.920
I was with on the street?

00:12:13.963 --> 00:12:15.988
You really should be
more careful out there.

00:12:16.032 --> 00:12:19.866
Those Mokra will pick
a fight for no reason.

00:12:19.902 --> 00:12:22.700
I don't want you
getting hurt... again.

00:12:23.706 --> 00:12:27.665
But I saw the way you
handled that ugly one.

00:12:29.979 --> 00:12:31.469
I couldn't have done any better.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:33.480
I was so proud of you, Ralkana.

00:12:33.549 --> 00:12:36.450
My two friends...
did the Mokra take them?

00:12:36.485 --> 00:12:37.611
I'm afraid so.

00:12:37.653 --> 00:12:39.382
Where would they
have been taken?

00:12:39.422 --> 00:12:40.514
A detention center?

00:12:43.025 --> 00:12:44.117
The prison.

00:12:45.328 --> 00:12:46.488
All right.

00:12:46.529 --> 00:12:47.723
How do I get there?

00:12:47.763 --> 00:12:49.287
Soup.

00:12:49.332 --> 00:12:50.697
I'm forgetting the soup.

00:12:50.733 --> 00:12:54.328
I appreciate your hospitality,
but I can't stay here.

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:55.803
I've got to get to that prison.

00:12:55.838 --> 00:12:57.237
You're right,
the time has come.

00:12:57.273 --> 00:13:00.868
Now we're together again,
we can't wait another day.

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:05.040
My beautiful and brave...
girl.

00:13:05.081 --> 00:13:08.244
The Mokra won't stand
a chance against us.

00:13:10.152 --> 00:13:12.416
You're very kind to offer,

00:13:12.455 --> 00:13:15.083
but I didn't mean
we'd be going together.

00:13:15.124 --> 00:13:21.120
You must eat and rest
to get your strength back.

00:13:21.163 --> 00:13:22.460
We'll leave soon enough.

00:13:22.531 --> 00:13:23.828
We don't want
to keep her waiting

00:13:23.866 --> 00:13:25.333
any longer than we have to.

00:13:29.271 --> 00:13:30.829
Keep who waiting?

00:13:32.308 --> 00:13:36.142
She must miss you so terribly.

00:13:36.178 --> 00:13:38.305
It's hard to bear...

00:13:38.347 --> 00:13:41.976
thinking of her alone
in that dark cell.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:46.012
It's been difficult
for all of us,

00:13:46.055 --> 00:13:49.684
but don't worry,
we'll get her out.

00:13:49.725 --> 00:13:52.125
You'll see your mother again.

00:14:03.239 --> 00:14:05.434
Our world has come
under attack before.

00:14:05.508 --> 00:14:07.840
You can understand our concern

00:14:07.877 --> 00:14:11.074
at finding strangers
who arrive secretly

00:14:11.113 --> 00:14:13.104
from a hidden ship.

00:14:13.149 --> 00:14:16.141
I assure you, we have
no hostile intentions.

00:14:16.185 --> 00:14:19.416
I believe you,
but some of my colleagues

00:14:19.455 --> 00:14:23.050
are cautious
about dealing with...

00:14:23.092 --> 00:14:24.559
disreputable ships.

00:14:24.593 --> 00:14:26.322
What does that mean?

00:14:28.264 --> 00:14:30.994
It seems you've been making
more enemies than friends

00:14:31.033 --> 00:14:32.466
since you arrived from the...

00:14:32.535 --> 00:14:34.400
Alpha Quadrant, is it?

00:14:34.437 --> 00:14:37.565
Some think even that story
is a lie.

00:14:37.606 --> 00:14:38.630
But not you.

00:14:38.674 --> 00:14:39.936
Of course not.

00:14:39.975 --> 00:14:41.602
I am here to help.

00:14:43.379 --> 00:14:45.779
Then I'd like to talk
to my crew members.

00:14:45.815 --> 00:14:47.840
I'm afraid
that will be difficult

00:14:47.883 --> 00:14:50.215
in the current climate
of mistrust.

00:14:50.252 --> 00:14:52.880
Perhaps if you could tell us

00:14:52.922 --> 00:14:54.412
more about
what brought you here...

00:14:54.457 --> 00:14:56.482
who you've been dealing with.

00:14:56.592 --> 00:14:58.685
I'll consider that

00:14:58.727 --> 00:15:00.695
after I talk to my crew members.

00:15:00.729 --> 00:15:04.790
You're not making it very easy
for me to help you.

00:15:09.572 --> 00:15:12.200
Let me see what I can arrange.

00:15:12.241 --> 00:15:14.232
It may take some time.

00:15:14.276 --> 00:15:15.300
Commander.

00:15:23.018 --> 00:15:25.009
Talk to your contacts again.

00:15:25.053 --> 00:15:26.714
I want an alternative
to sitting here

00:15:26.755 --> 00:15:28.313
waiting for him
to get back to us.

00:15:30.892 --> 00:15:33.360
Your question is based
on a faulty assumption.

00:15:33.395 --> 00:15:34.794
I cannot answer it.

00:15:34.829 --> 00:15:36.057
You can't deny

00:15:36.097 --> 00:15:38.565
being in contact
with the resistance.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:41.398
I deny that we are intending
to supply them with weapons.

00:15:41.436 --> 00:15:43.700
These lies are useless.

00:15:43.738 --> 00:15:46.070
We know you're helping
the subversives.

00:15:46.107 --> 00:15:48.803
I want names.

00:15:48.843 --> 00:15:50.367
I have none to give you.

00:15:50.412 --> 00:15:52.107
He told you already...
we don't know anything

00:15:52.147 --> 00:15:53.614
about the resistance!

00:15:53.648 --> 00:15:58.381
I've heard that many times
from many people.

00:15:58.420 --> 00:15:59.887
Take him.

00:16:01.756 --> 00:16:03.917
Lieutenant, stop!

00:16:03.958 --> 00:16:05.789
That will not help either of us.

00:16:05.827 --> 00:16:07.624
He's right.

00:16:21.176 --> 00:16:22.108
Open up!

00:16:22.143 --> 00:16:23.110
No!

00:16:23.144 --> 00:16:24.406
Break it down!

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:29.448
I see soldiers out there.

00:16:29.551 --> 00:16:30.848
What's happening?

00:16:30.885 --> 00:16:32.147
They're everywhere...

00:16:32.187 --> 00:16:33.176
searching the whole area.

00:16:33.221 --> 00:16:34.449
I don't want to cause
trouble for you.

00:16:34.489 --> 00:16:35.751
I'll go soon as it's dark.

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:37.223
You've always been
a troublemaker

00:16:37.258 --> 00:16:38.452
ever since you could walk.

00:16:38.493 --> 00:16:40.586
I've never seen
such a willful child.

00:16:40.628 --> 00:16:42.459
But that's what I love
most about you...

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:43.554
your spirit.

00:16:43.598 --> 00:16:44.690
Now, don't worry.

00:16:44.733 --> 00:16:47.634
When they come through here,
we'll be gone already.

00:16:47.669 --> 00:16:51.833
Now, your mother will want
some of her things.

00:16:53.875 --> 00:16:56.935
Ah... a pretty dress to wear.

00:16:58.012 --> 00:16:59.479
They're only looking for me.

00:16:59.581 --> 00:17:01.139
You don't have to get
any more involved

00:17:01.182 --> 00:17:02.308
than you already are.

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:04.181
Why, if my precious girl
is involved

00:17:04.219 --> 00:17:05.447
then I'm involved, too.

00:17:14.129 --> 00:17:15.756
Do you remember this?

00:17:15.797 --> 00:17:18.425
She always used to wear it
on special occasions.

00:17:18.466 --> 00:17:22.425
I think today
would count... as one.

00:17:22.537 --> 00:17:25.563
You know what I think
she would like even more...

00:17:28.209 --> 00:17:30.268
is to see you wear it.

00:17:30.311 --> 00:17:31.608
I couldn't possibly take it...

00:17:31.646 --> 00:17:33.876
Be careful, be careful
this won't heal

00:17:33.915 --> 00:17:35.542
if you move around too much.

00:17:35.583 --> 00:17:37.949
If you want to help,
tell me about that prison.

00:17:37.986 --> 00:17:39.544
What kind of security
do they have?

00:17:39.587 --> 00:17:40.645
Are there force fields,

00:17:40.688 --> 00:17:42.280
detection grids,
physical barriers?

00:17:42.323 --> 00:17:44.314
Yes, all of it.

00:17:44.359 --> 00:17:45.348
What about guards?

00:17:45.393 --> 00:17:46.724
Lots of guards.

00:17:46.761 --> 00:17:49.787
The Mokra make
a big show of it...

00:17:49.831 --> 00:17:54.131
always bragging about how no one
has ever escaped.

00:17:54.169 --> 00:17:56.103
Listen to me...

00:17:56.137 --> 00:17:59.004
I can't bring you
to the prison with me.

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:01.304
It's too dangerous.

00:18:04.078 --> 00:18:05.306
I'm not afraid.

00:18:05.346 --> 00:18:07.507
And that could get
both of us killed.

00:18:07.549 --> 00:18:09.608
You have to stay here.

00:18:09.651 --> 00:18:13.519
If I stay here I can't
bring the letters.

00:18:13.555 --> 00:18:15.819
Letters... to the prison?

00:18:15.857 --> 00:18:17.222
Letters.

00:18:17.258 --> 00:18:19.624
Don't you remember
how we used to write

00:18:19.661 --> 00:18:21.219
to her together?

00:18:27.902 --> 00:18:29.893
Here they are.

00:18:29.938 --> 00:18:31.667
I still write them...

00:18:31.706 --> 00:18:33.105
every week
since she's been gone.

00:18:33.141 --> 00:18:35.701
I've always known that one day

00:18:35.743 --> 00:18:38.576
I'd be able to...
to give them to her.

00:18:38.613 --> 00:18:40.547
I've never forgotten.

00:18:40.582 --> 00:18:42.982
These are all to your wife?

00:18:43.017 --> 00:18:45.110
How long has it been?

00:18:45.153 --> 00:18:47.587
My last letter...

00:18:49.858 --> 00:18:51.883
my last letter's not...

00:18:51.926 --> 00:18:53.951
it's not here.

00:18:53.995 --> 00:18:59.661
Oh, I wrote it three days ago,
but it's... it's not...

00:18:59.701 --> 00:19:03.000
I can't let her think
I've stopped writing...

00:19:03.037 --> 00:19:08.065
that I gave up hope only,
only days before...

00:19:08.109 --> 00:19:11.237
Huh, I'll write it again.

00:19:17.051 --> 00:19:18.985
My hand...

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:21.648
my hand shakes sometimes.

00:19:21.689 --> 00:19:23.213
You write it so it looks nice.

00:19:23.258 --> 00:19:27.592
I'm very sorry, I have to go
before the soldiers come.

00:19:27.629 --> 00:19:31.998
The last one...
the last one was about...

00:19:34.135 --> 00:19:37.434
My memory isn't very good.

00:19:37.538 --> 00:19:39.438
No, I remember.

00:19:39.507 --> 00:19:42.101
I went walking in the morning.

00:19:42.143 --> 00:19:46.170
It was... it was very cold.

00:19:46.214 --> 00:19:49.149
Tell her I wore my sweater.

00:19:49.183 --> 00:19:53.449
She worries
about that sort of... thing.

00:19:53.521 --> 00:19:58.390
And... and, uh...

00:19:58.426 --> 00:20:01.623
and I, uh, and I what?

00:20:03.965 --> 00:20:06.798
And I saw they had torn down
that old building

00:20:06.834 --> 00:20:10.634
where you and the other children
used to... to play.

00:20:10.672 --> 00:20:15.132
And, uh... what?

00:20:15.176 --> 00:20:19.169
Tell her that it rained
for two and a half days.

00:20:19.213 --> 00:20:22.114
I don't know
if she can see the sky...

00:20:24.419 --> 00:20:26.319
where they're keeping her.

00:20:29.757 --> 00:20:33.193
And... there was more.

00:20:33.227 --> 00:20:38.790
There was something
about a friend... I...

00:20:38.833 --> 00:20:39.959
Why can't I remember?

00:20:40.001 --> 00:20:41.628
I wanted to tell her!

00:20:45.206 --> 00:20:49.165
It's all right.
She'll understand.

00:20:51.512 --> 00:20:55.073
Yes, yes, you're right.

00:20:55.116 --> 00:20:56.879
She will.

00:21:06.294 --> 00:21:09.286
Please let me come with you.

00:21:10.298 --> 00:21:13.358
I'm sorry;
that's not possible.

00:21:13.401 --> 00:21:14.663
Check this one here!

00:21:15.603 --> 00:21:16.934
Is there another way out?

00:21:16.971 --> 00:21:18.268
Open up or else!

00:21:18.306 --> 00:21:20.240
There.

00:21:23.611 --> 00:21:25.169
Open the door!

00:21:25.213 --> 00:21:26.737
Open the door now!

00:21:26.781 --> 00:21:28.612
Break it down!

00:22:10.524 --> 00:22:12.458
This is a waste of time.

00:22:12.492 --> 00:22:13.925
We don't need him anyway.

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:15.086
I need him.

00:22:15.128 --> 00:22:16.959
If he's a member
of the resistance,

00:22:16.997 --> 00:22:19.363
he may be able to help
me contact my ship.

00:22:21.968 --> 00:22:23.902
Monster!

00:22:28.775 --> 00:22:31.209
He's the one.
He took your mother.

00:22:31.244 --> 00:22:32.211
We have to...

00:22:32.245 --> 00:22:35.112
They want a fight.

00:22:35.148 --> 00:22:37.241
Don't give them one.

00:22:41.054 --> 00:22:44.182
What? I've done nothing!
I've done nothing.

00:22:44.224 --> 00:22:45.282
Please!

00:22:45.325 --> 00:22:46.314
Please...

00:22:47.027 --> 00:22:48.324
You look like a helpful citizen.

00:22:48.361 --> 00:22:49.328
So, tell me.

00:22:49.362 --> 00:22:51.956
You might have seen
some strangers

00:22:51.998 --> 00:22:54.262
who were in the marketplace
earlier today.

00:22:54.301 --> 00:22:56.792
No, sir.
No, I've seen no one.

00:22:56.836 --> 00:22:57.666
Please.

00:22:57.704 --> 00:22:58.693
You!

00:23:07.447 --> 00:23:10.075
I'm looking for someone,
a woman.

00:23:10.116 --> 00:23:12.175
I haven't seen any woman.

00:23:14.254 --> 00:23:16.950
There are two right over here.

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:19.458
You see them, don't you?

00:23:19.526 --> 00:23:20.550
Yes.

00:23:20.594 --> 00:23:22.892
Maybe we should discuss
this elsewhere.

00:23:25.966 --> 00:23:27.456
Caylem...

00:23:29.836 --> 00:23:30.803
Good morning.

00:23:33.573 --> 00:23:35.336
I seem to have lost my hat.

00:23:40.914 --> 00:23:43.712
It's about this... this big.

00:23:59.833 --> 00:24:01.960
Have you seen my hat?

00:24:04.938 --> 00:24:06.667
Run along, old man.

00:24:06.706 --> 00:24:09.038
Without my hat?

00:24:19.986 --> 00:24:21.044
There you go.

00:24:48.648 --> 00:24:53.381
There... it's...
it's all right now.

00:24:53.420 --> 00:24:54.717
They've gone.

00:25:31.491 --> 00:25:33.925
The prison is in the northeast
corner of the city.

00:25:33.960 --> 00:25:34.927
My sources tell me

00:25:34.961 --> 00:25:37.862
it's surrounded
by metaphasic shields.

00:25:37.897 --> 00:25:39.330
Can we find a way
to beam through them?

00:25:39.365 --> 00:25:41.629
The Mokra aren't familiar
with transporter technology.

00:25:41.668 --> 00:25:45.468
There is a periodic fluctuation
in the shield's energy pattern.

00:25:45.572 --> 00:25:47.199
I'm working on a way
to take advantage of it.

00:25:47.240 --> 00:25:48.867
There's only one problem
with that.

00:25:48.908 --> 00:25:51.103
If the Mokra detect us
breaking through their shields,

00:25:51.144 --> 00:25:53.169
we'll be surrounded
by soldiers in seconds.

00:25:53.213 --> 00:25:54.805
If we could beam in
close enough

00:25:54.848 --> 00:25:56.782
to where the away team
is being held,

00:25:56.816 --> 00:25:57.874
we might be able to get
in and out of there

00:25:57.917 --> 00:25:59.782
before the Mokra
had a chance to react.

00:25:59.819 --> 00:26:02.310
We can't locate
the away team from here.

00:26:02.355 --> 00:26:04.346
The detention level
is subterranean

00:26:04.390 --> 00:26:07.621
and the rock is too dense
for our sensors to penetrate.

00:26:07.660 --> 00:26:10.254
You'll have to look for them
after you beam into the prison.

00:26:10.296 --> 00:26:11.422
Too dangerous.

00:26:11.464 --> 00:26:12.931
We can't risk beaming in.

00:26:12.966 --> 00:26:15.628
We'll have to find another way
that the Mokra won't detect.

00:26:15.668 --> 00:26:17.761
Sounds like a challenge
for you, Mr. Kim.

00:26:20.340 --> 00:26:21.807
You'd be welcome
to use our transmitter

00:26:21.841 --> 00:26:23.240
if we still had one.

00:26:23.276 --> 00:26:25.005
The Mokra confiscated
it this morning.

00:26:25.044 --> 00:26:26.534
Then I'll have to find
my crew members myself.

00:26:26.579 --> 00:26:28.376
I know two of them
were arrested.

00:26:28.414 --> 00:26:29.438
What about Neelix?

00:26:29.482 --> 00:26:30.414
He stayed inside with me,

00:26:30.450 --> 00:26:31.917
then got transported
up to your ship.

00:26:31.951 --> 00:26:34.647
Good. What can you tell me
about the prison?

00:26:34.687 --> 00:26:35.745
I know about the prison.

00:26:35.789 --> 00:26:37.222
We need all the information
we can get.

00:26:37.257 --> 00:26:38.383
I have to reach my crew.

00:26:38.424 --> 00:26:39.789
Don't you think there
are people in there

00:26:39.826 --> 00:26:40.850
I'd like to get out?

00:26:40.894 --> 00:26:42.725
Any sane person would
tell you it's impossible.

00:26:42.762 --> 00:26:44.593
Spoken like a coward.

00:26:44.631 --> 00:26:46.098
I've heard about you, old man.

00:26:46.132 --> 00:26:47.156
You're the coward!

00:26:47.200 --> 00:26:48.462
Enough.

00:26:48.535 --> 00:26:50.469
What are you doing
with this lunatic?

00:26:50.537 --> 00:26:52.767
Has he been telling you stories
of his brave deeds?

00:26:52.806 --> 00:26:53.830
They're just fantasies.

00:26:53.873 --> 00:26:54.840
Taking him along

00:26:54.874 --> 00:26:56.671
on this rescue mission
of yours is suicide.

00:26:56.709 --> 00:26:59.143
He's already saved me
from the Mokra once.

00:26:59.179 --> 00:27:01.807
And he saved you from
those soldiers today.

00:27:01.848 --> 00:27:03.213
All right, stay with him.

00:27:03.249 --> 00:27:05.240
Go off to the prison,
get yourself killed.

00:27:05.285 --> 00:27:08.049
I don't have to get killed
if you'll tell me what you know.

00:27:09.322 --> 00:27:10.880
There are access tunnels
on the north side.

00:27:10.924 --> 00:27:12.221
They'll get you in
a little closer,

00:27:12.258 --> 00:27:13.225
but they're guarded.

00:27:13.259 --> 00:27:14.385
Then I'll need weapons.

00:27:14.427 --> 00:27:16.224
They're not free.

00:27:16.262 --> 00:27:18.059
I don't have anything to trade.

00:27:18.097 --> 00:27:20.031
That's worth some weapons.

00:27:20.066 --> 00:27:21.727
I can't.

00:27:21.768 --> 00:27:23.599
Yes, you can...

00:27:23.636 --> 00:27:26.537
if it'll help
to bring her back to us.

00:27:26.573 --> 00:27:28.404
Thank you.

00:27:28.441 --> 00:27:30.739
I can have someone
meet you on the street

00:27:30.777 --> 00:27:32.608
in three hours
to make the trade.

00:27:32.645 --> 00:27:34.237
He'll be wearing a blue vest.

00:27:34.280 --> 00:27:35.304
Watch for him.

00:27:35.348 --> 00:27:37.316
We will. Thank you.

00:27:37.350 --> 00:27:38.942
I'd wish you luck,

00:27:38.985 --> 00:27:40.953
but what you'll need
is a miracle.

00:27:57.703 --> 00:28:00.297
He's more than three hours late.

00:28:00.339 --> 00:28:02.170
We have to consider
the possibility

00:28:02.208 --> 00:28:03.539
that he's been arrested.

00:28:05.011 --> 00:28:07.411
You mustn't believe
what he told you about me.

00:28:08.848 --> 00:28:10.406
I don't believe it.

00:28:10.483 --> 00:28:12.747
You're not a coward.

00:28:14.587 --> 00:28:16.145
I had to keep
my little girl safe.

00:28:16.188 --> 00:28:18.179
It was just too dangerous
to get involved.

00:28:18.224 --> 00:28:19.885
Can you understand?

00:28:19.926 --> 00:28:21.587
Your mother wouldn't listen.

00:28:21.627 --> 00:28:23.788
She wanted to fight.

00:28:23.829 --> 00:28:28.425
She was always... so passionate
about what she believed in.

00:28:28.501 --> 00:28:30.366
She didn't care about the risk.

00:28:31.804 --> 00:28:33.772
You were proud of her.

00:28:34.607 --> 00:28:36.802
I didn't want to lose her.

00:28:36.842 --> 00:28:40.141
I didn't want you to grow up
without a mother.

00:28:40.179 --> 00:28:43.808
I tried so hard
to change her mind

00:28:43.849 --> 00:28:46.215
and finally she changed mine.

00:28:46.252 --> 00:28:49.415
She convinced me to go with her.

00:28:50.756 --> 00:28:54.624
I said I would meet her...
by the river.

00:28:54.660 --> 00:28:58.994
She was leading a raid
against a Mokra supply center.

00:29:02.268 --> 00:29:03.963
I said I would meet her...

00:29:06.305 --> 00:29:08.603
but I didn't... I couldn't.

00:29:08.641 --> 00:29:10.131
I was too afraid.

00:29:14.280 --> 00:29:18.512
She was still waiting for me
when they arrested her.

00:29:18.551 --> 00:29:21.019
I could never tell you
about this.

00:29:21.053 --> 00:29:23.544
I knew you would hate me.

00:29:23.589 --> 00:29:25.420
I couldn't bear that.

00:29:25.491 --> 00:29:27.789
Please, Ralkana,
if you can ever forgive me...

00:29:34.233 --> 00:29:35.962
All right, I'll be right there.

00:29:45.945 --> 00:29:47.412
What is it?

00:29:47.446 --> 00:29:48.435
A blue vest.

00:29:48.547 --> 00:29:49.844
Then it's time to go.

00:30:17.610 --> 00:30:19.475
What happened?

00:30:19.578 --> 00:30:22.570
He was wearing military boots
like the Mokra.

00:30:22.615 --> 00:30:23.582
It was a trap.

00:30:23.616 --> 00:30:25.243
A trap?
And you saw it?

00:30:25.284 --> 00:30:26.410
My clever girl.

00:30:26.452 --> 00:30:27.180
We'll be all right.

00:30:27.219 --> 00:30:28.186
We have each other.

00:30:28.220 --> 00:30:29.187
That's all we'll need.

00:30:29.221 --> 00:30:30.245
It's not that simple.

00:30:30.289 --> 00:30:32.883
We can't just walk
into the prison without weapons.

00:30:42.034 --> 00:30:44.969
Maybe we'll have to try
a different strategy.

00:30:57.416 --> 00:31:00.351
We don't have to ask your friend
any more questions

00:31:00.386 --> 00:31:02.115
if you give us the answers.

00:31:02.154 --> 00:31:04.782
I told you, I don't...

00:31:19.205 --> 00:31:21.139
I'm sorry.

00:31:32.451 --> 00:31:35.113
I guess I... I always assumed

00:31:35.154 --> 00:31:40.023
that Vulcans didn't feel pain
like the rest of us;

00:31:40.059 --> 00:31:44.018
that you were able
to block it out somehow

00:31:44.063 --> 00:31:45.724
until I heard...

00:31:47.099 --> 00:31:48.862
Was that you I heard?

00:31:51.303 --> 00:31:55.330
Vulcans are capable
of suppressing

00:31:55.374 --> 00:31:58.969
certain levels of physical pain.

00:31:59.011 --> 00:32:05.780
Beyond that, we must simply
endure the experience.

00:32:05.818 --> 00:32:08.150
How can you say that so calmly?

00:32:08.187 --> 00:32:14.422
You must feel some anger
at what they did to you...

00:32:14.460 --> 00:32:16.451
some desire to fight back.

00:32:17.997 --> 00:32:20.261
Under the circumstances,

00:32:20.299 --> 00:32:23.757
physical resistance
is ineffective.

00:32:23.803 --> 00:32:28.604
We are... fighting back

00:32:28.641 --> 00:32:32.475
by refusing to give
them any information.

00:32:33.946 --> 00:32:35.140
Get down there!

00:32:47.426 --> 00:32:49.860
Three more hours.

00:32:51.030 --> 00:32:53.260
There's nothing
going on around here.

00:32:53.299 --> 00:32:55.392
Wake me if the Lieutenant
shows up, will you?

00:33:14.253 --> 00:33:17.745
You girls aren't supposed
to come down here anymore.

00:33:18.924 --> 00:33:20.482
Do you want me to leave?

00:33:25.331 --> 00:33:27.356
I didn't say that.

00:33:29.335 --> 00:33:31.860
Then I won't.

00:33:31.904 --> 00:33:34.873
If my Lieutenant saw you here,
I'd be in trouble.

00:33:36.208 --> 00:33:39.143
Nobody will see us back here.

00:33:40.713 --> 00:33:42.613
It's dark...

00:33:42.648 --> 00:33:44.047
private.

00:34:04.503 --> 00:34:05.868
I like this strategy.

00:34:24.290 --> 00:34:25.382
Ready to go?

00:34:25.424 --> 00:34:27.654
No... you're not coming with me.

00:34:27.693 --> 00:34:29.160
Of course I am.

00:34:29.194 --> 00:34:31.458
We settled this.

00:34:31.563 --> 00:34:34.031
You told that man, Darod,

00:34:34.066 --> 00:34:36.296
how I saved you from the Mokra!

00:34:36.335 --> 00:34:37.597
You did save me.

00:34:37.636 --> 00:34:39.365
Now I'm returning the favor.

00:34:43.108 --> 00:34:46.339
I promise I'll try
to find your wife.

00:34:48.781 --> 00:34:49.975
Wait!

00:34:50.015 --> 00:34:51.243
Ralkana!

00:34:51.283 --> 00:34:53.012
No!

00:34:57.423 --> 00:34:59.584
I've been studying
their orbital sensor net.

00:34:59.625 --> 00:35:01.217
It surrounds the entire planet.

00:35:01.260 --> 00:35:03.751
This is the most sophisticated
system I've ever seen.

00:35:03.796 --> 00:35:07.163
It monitors everything we do,
there's no way of disabling

00:35:07.199 --> 00:35:08.188
it from orbit.

00:35:08.233 --> 00:35:09.996
So much for a surprise attack.

00:35:10.035 --> 00:35:11.332
We may still be able
to surprise them

00:35:11.370 --> 00:35:12.428
even if they do see us coming.

00:35:12.471 --> 00:35:15.634
We could modify
the main deflector

00:35:15.674 --> 00:35:16.971
to send out dozens
of radion beams

00:35:17.009 --> 00:35:18.670
which should penetrate
the prison shields.

00:35:18.711 --> 00:35:20.645
One of them will carry
our transporter signal,

00:35:20.679 --> 00:35:24.137
but the sensor net won't be
able to distinguish which one,

00:35:24.183 --> 00:35:25.309
so the Mokra won't know

00:35:25.351 --> 00:35:27.148
the exact location
we're beaming to.

00:35:27.186 --> 00:35:29.177
And they won't know where
to concentrate their defenses.

00:35:29.221 --> 00:35:30.882
That's the best head start
I can give you.

00:35:30.923 --> 00:35:31.890
Then it'll have to do.

00:35:31.924 --> 00:35:34.222
How long will it take to modify
the deflector?

00:35:34.259 --> 00:35:35.726
I can do it right now.

00:35:35.761 --> 00:35:37.956
Chakotay to Paris.
Is the rescue team ready?

00:35:37.997 --> 00:35:38.964
Standing by.

00:35:38.998 --> 00:35:40.295
Prepare for transport.

00:35:40.332 --> 00:35:42.163
Deflector ready, Commander.

00:35:42.201 --> 00:35:43.828
Initiate the radion beams.

00:35:43.869 --> 00:35:45.734
Sending out the first volley...

00:35:45.771 --> 00:35:47.238
It's working.

00:35:47.272 --> 00:35:48.569
They're getting
through the shields.

00:35:48.607 --> 00:35:49.904
Begin the transport.

00:35:49.942 --> 00:35:51.307
Transporter Room 2,

00:35:51.343 --> 00:35:53.402
synchronize
your confinement beams to...

00:35:54.847 --> 00:35:56.246
That came from the surface.

00:35:56.281 --> 00:35:57.407
Maximum shields.

00:35:57.449 --> 00:35:58.279
Damage report.

00:35:58.317 --> 00:35:59.807
Shields at 90 percent.

00:35:59.852 --> 00:36:02.878
That was a precision hit right
to the source of the beams.

00:36:02.921 --> 00:36:05.321
Main deflector is now off-line.

00:36:06.358 --> 00:36:07.882
We're being hailed
from the surface.

00:36:07.926 --> 00:36:09.188
On screen.

00:36:10.896 --> 00:36:12.989
Your attempt
to penetrate our defenses

00:36:13.032 --> 00:36:16.229
is a hostile act
against the Mokra Order.

00:36:16.268 --> 00:36:18.930
There are now
85 phased-ion cannons

00:36:18.971 --> 00:36:20.632
targeted at your ship.

00:36:20.672 --> 00:36:24.005
If you don't withdraw
from Mokra space in two minutes,

00:36:24.043 --> 00:36:26.375
we will open fire.

00:37:34.613 --> 00:37:36.103
Commander.

00:37:36.147 --> 00:37:38.081
Give me some good news, Mr. Kim.

00:37:38.116 --> 00:37:40.448
There's a disruption in the
shields around the prison.

00:37:40.485 --> 00:37:41.952
That qualifies.
Good work.

00:37:41.987 --> 00:37:43.386
I wish I could take
credit for it,

00:37:43.421 --> 00:37:45.116
but it's coming
from inside the prison.

00:37:45.156 --> 00:37:46.180
Can we get through?

00:37:46.224 --> 00:37:49.091
Yes, but the Mokra
will detect our transport.

00:37:49.127 --> 00:37:51.220
Sounds like they have other
things to worry about right now.

00:37:51.262 --> 00:37:54.197
That disruption might
not be accidental.

00:37:54.232 --> 00:37:56.462
Someone in there might
be trying to get out.

00:37:56.501 --> 00:37:57.661
That's a big assumption.

00:37:57.702 --> 00:38:00.671
Even if our people
didn't cause the problem,

00:38:00.705 --> 00:38:02.605
you know they'd take
advantage of it.

00:38:03.642 --> 00:38:05.803
This is our best chance
to find them.

00:38:05.844 --> 00:38:08.335
In about 30 seconds, the Mokra
are going to open fire.

00:38:08.380 --> 00:38:10.575
I don't know how long we'll
be able to wait for you.

00:38:10.615 --> 00:38:12.207
Understood.

00:38:22.494 --> 00:38:24.086
Darod.

00:38:26.331 --> 00:38:28.162
I'm looking for my people.

00:38:28.199 --> 00:38:29.564
Back this way.

00:38:29.601 --> 00:38:31.091
I'll show you.

00:38:58.163 --> 00:39:00.131
Don't move.

00:39:01.766 --> 00:39:02.733
There you are.

00:39:02.767 --> 00:39:04.132
What are you doing here?

00:39:04.169 --> 00:39:06.399
I would do everything
in my power

00:39:06.504 --> 00:39:08.734
to protect my only child.

00:39:13.978 --> 00:39:16.310
There's a phased-ion charge
coming at us from the planet.

00:39:16.347 --> 00:39:18.110
Full power to the shields.

00:39:18.149 --> 00:39:22.085
Shields at 60 percent.
Minor damage on Deck 14.

00:39:22.120 --> 00:39:23.610
They're firing again.

00:39:23.655 --> 00:39:24.644
Modulate the shield frequencies.

00:39:24.689 --> 00:39:25.883
Try to throw off their sensors.

00:39:30.195 --> 00:39:31.526
No effect.

00:39:31.563 --> 00:39:33.224
Direct hit to the port nacelle.

00:39:33.264 --> 00:39:35.198
Redirect all warp power
to the shields.

00:39:36.401 --> 00:39:37.959
Two more coming in.

00:39:44.776 --> 00:39:45.401
Captain.

00:39:47.445 --> 00:39:49.436
We've got to get you
back to the ship.

00:39:49.547 --> 00:39:50.605
You're hurt.

00:39:50.648 --> 00:39:53.048
Ralkana, the other cells
are this way.

00:39:53.084 --> 00:39:54.346
We must find your mother.

00:39:57.055 --> 00:39:58.022
Follow this passageway

00:39:58.056 --> 00:39:59.318
until it dead-ends.

00:39:59.357 --> 00:40:00.790
Then you'll see
a smaller passageway.

00:40:00.825 --> 00:40:02.383
Captain, what are you doing?

00:40:02.427 --> 00:40:04.622
There's one more person
I have to find.

00:40:04.662 --> 00:40:05.651
Guards!

00:40:10.702 --> 00:40:14.069
After all that time
I spent looking for you,

00:40:14.105 --> 00:40:17.006
all I had to do was wait here.

00:40:21.613 --> 00:40:22.671
Shields down to 23 percent.

00:40:22.714 --> 00:40:24.875
We've got to get out
of their weapons range.

00:40:24.916 --> 00:40:26.907
Scan one more time
for the away team.

00:40:27.886 --> 00:40:29.751
There's no sign of them.

00:40:31.222 --> 00:40:32.382
Prepare to break orbit.

00:40:33.625 --> 00:40:37.186
Wait! Set a course
bearing 219 mark 47.

00:40:37.228 --> 00:40:39.321
Where are you taking us,
Mr. Kim?

00:40:40.598 --> 00:40:43.066
There's a large electrical storm
over the northern magnetic pole.

00:40:43.101 --> 00:40:44.966
It's giving our sensors
some trouble.

00:40:45.003 --> 00:40:45.970
It should do the same
for theirs.

00:40:46.004 --> 00:40:47.972
- A blind spot.
- Exactly.

00:40:48.006 --> 00:40:50.440
If we maintain our position
directly above the storm,

00:40:50.475 --> 00:40:53.103
their sensor net may not be able
to keep an accurate lock

00:40:53.144 --> 00:40:54.111
on our position.

00:40:54.145 --> 00:40:55.112
How long do you think
this'll work?

00:40:55.146 --> 00:40:56.613
The storm's already dissipating.

00:40:56.648 --> 00:40:57.512
A few more minutes?

00:40:57.615 --> 00:40:59.048
I'll take every second
I can get.

00:41:00.785 --> 00:41:03.811
I must say I'm impressed,
Caylem.

00:41:03.855 --> 00:41:06.221
You never made it
this far before.

00:41:06.257 --> 00:41:10.455
Every so often, he goes on one
of his missions...

00:41:10.528 --> 00:41:13.326
to rescue his wife.

00:41:13.364 --> 00:41:15.730
She's been dead for 12 years.

00:41:15.767 --> 00:41:17.394
Lies.

00:41:17.435 --> 00:41:19.460
Lies... lies!

00:41:19.504 --> 00:41:23.270
Sometimes... he gets all
the way up to the front gate.

00:41:23.308 --> 00:41:25.708
We send him on his way

00:41:25.743 --> 00:41:27.870
and allow him
to serve as a reminder

00:41:27.912 --> 00:41:31.075
of just how futile it is
to challenge us.

00:41:31.115 --> 00:41:32.742
I thought
you'd learned that lesson

00:41:32.784 --> 00:41:34.149
when you lost your daughter.

00:41:34.185 --> 00:41:38.087
She made it as far as the
tunnels before she was shot.

00:41:38.122 --> 00:41:39.214
No!

00:41:39.257 --> 00:41:42.715
So much tragedy
for one man to bear...

00:41:42.760 --> 00:41:46.423
and now your foolishness
has condemned

00:41:46.464 --> 00:41:48.455
another innocent woman.

00:41:49.968 --> 00:41:51.799
Take the others back
for questioning.

00:41:51.836 --> 00:41:54.396
I'll interrogate this one
myself.

00:41:54.439 --> 00:41:56.100
No! I won't let you hurt her!

00:42:13.591 --> 00:42:15.081
Caylem!

00:42:32.977 --> 00:42:34.740
Ralkana...

00:42:36.848 --> 00:42:39.408
he said you'd been shot.

00:42:39.450 --> 00:42:43.784
He was lying to you, Father.

00:42:43.821 --> 00:42:45.482
I'm all right.

00:42:46.891 --> 00:42:48.586
And your mother?

00:42:48.626 --> 00:42:50.184
She's fine.

00:42:50.228 --> 00:42:53.288
She was so happy
to get your letters.

00:42:57.669 --> 00:43:00.137
She wanted me
to tell you something.

00:43:00.171 --> 00:43:02.435
She forgives you.

00:43:02.507 --> 00:43:04.873
We both do.

00:43:15.353 --> 00:43:17.617
My sweet girl.

00:43:38.376 --> 00:43:39.707
Captain.

00:43:41.512 --> 00:43:42.672
I'm coming.

00:43:54.058 --> 00:43:56.686
No one will forget
what he did here today.

00:43:56.728 --> 00:43:58.525
I'll make sure of that.

00:44:02.433 --> 00:44:03.923
Chakotay to Transporter Room 2.

00:44:03.968 --> 00:44:04.957
Do we have them?

00:44:05.003 --> 00:44:06.436
We're all back, Commander.

00:44:06.471 --> 00:44:07.438
Take us out of here.

00:44:07.538 --> 00:44:09.938
Gladly.

00:44:09.974 --> 00:44:11.498
Lieutenant, you heard her.

00:44:17.749 --> 00:44:20.013
The warp drive is
functioning normally,

00:44:20.051 --> 00:44:24.750
and we'll have the main
deflector back on line tomorrow.

00:44:26.591 --> 00:44:28.149
Yes, thank you, Mr. Kim.

00:44:29.160 --> 00:44:31.128
Captain, are you all right?

00:44:31.162 --> 00:44:32.220
I'm fine.
